IMPORT prelude

-- Magistrates Court (Civil Proceedings) Act 2004 (Western Australia) -- whether a consumer can bring a small claim as a
-- minor case, and what the minor cases procedure means for them.
--
-- SEAT: the consumer claimant ("Can I bring a minor case for a small claim? Can the Magistrates Court hear my claim at all?
-- What does the minor cases procedure mean for me: may I have a lawyer, what costs can I win or be made to pay, are the
-- rules of evidence applied, and can I appeal?"). Every exported question is phrased as that person would ask it. What the
-- Act tells the Court to do is encoded as what it means for the claimant: whether their claim is heard, how, by whom they
-- may be represented, and what costs can be ordered for or against them.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3 (minor cases jurisdictional limit, $10 000 on and after 1 January 2009); s 4 (jurisdictional
-- limit, $75 000 on and after 1 January 2009); s 6(1)(a), (b), (d), (e), (f), (g) and (5) (general civil jurisdiction and
-- the claims the Court cannot hear); s 7 (consumer, trader, consumer/trader claim); s 10(2) (interest disregarded); s 16(1)(j)
-- (a case under the minor limit may be ordered into the minor cases procedure; noted); s 25(1), (2), (5) (costs; the minor
-- case costs rule follows the claim's value); s 26 (minor case); s 27 (settlement first); s 28 (minor cases procedure or
-- general procedure); s 29 (private and informal; rules of evidence do not bind); s 30 (representation in a minor case);
-- s 31 (allowable costs); s 32 (appeals from a minor case); s 40(1), (3) (appeal to the District Court, 21 days); s 44(1),
-- (2)(a), (d), (3) (representation in a case that is not a minor case); s 45(1) (open court).
--
-- Edition: the Magistrates Court (Civil Proceedings) Act 2004 (No. 48 of 2004), compilation as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48918.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 48918, retrieved 2026-09-07); its s 7 carries
-- the amendment by No. 21 of 2023 (Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023). No regulations or rules of court
-- are used: neither the Magistrates Court (Civil Proceedings) Regulations nor the Magistrates Court (Civil Proceedings)
-- Rules are deposited, so the proceedings "prescribed by the regulations" (s 30(3)(a)) and the time for an appeal from a
-- registrar to a magistrate (s 32(2)(b)) are inputs or are answered as not encoded.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the limits before 1 January 2009 ($7 500 and $50 000); s 6(1)(a)(ii), (iii) (partnership accounts and shares
-- under an intestacy or will, folded into "an amount of money"); s 6(2)-(4) (partnership powers; how gross annual rental
-- value is worked out: asked as a figure); s 8 (jurisdiction under other Acts) and s 26(b) (minor cases declared by another
-- Act); s 9 (counterclaims outside jurisdiction) and s 28(4) (a counterclaim that is not a minor case); ss 11, 12 (remedies,
-- prejudgment interest); ss 13-24 (general procedure and case management) except s 16(1)(j); s 25(3), (4), (6)-(12)
-- (costs machinery, wasted costs against lawyers); s 30(2)(a) (corporations and public officers); s 30(6)-(9); s 33;
-- Parts 5 (mediation), 6 (transfer to a superior court), 7 beyond s 40(1), (3); ss 41-43; s 46 (enforcement); ss 47-49.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the consumer claimant, with the design
-- defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use
-- as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Conventions. Money is in dollars. "My claim" is the claim the claimant starts; the amount is the amount claimed after any
-- payment on account or admitted setoff, and without interest (ss 6(1)(a), 10(2)).

§ `Magistrates Court (Civil Proceedings) Act 2004 -- the consumer claimant`

§§ `ss 3, 4 -- the two limits`

-- s 3(1): "minor cases jurisdictional limit means $7 500 and, on and after 1 January 2009, means $10 000".
-- s 4: "jurisdictional limit means $50 000 and, on and after 1 January 2009, means $75 000".
-- Only the figures in force on and after 1 January 2009 are encoded.
@export What is the most I can claim as a minor case (s 3, minor cases jurisdictional limit)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the minor cases jurisdictional limit` IS 10000

@export What is the most the Magistrates Court can hear in an ordinary money claim (s 4, jurisdictional limit)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the jurisdictional limit` IS 75000

§§ `My claim -- the facts`

-- s 6(1): the kinds of claim the Court has jurisdiction to deal with.
DECLARE `What I am claiming` IS ONE OF
    `an amount of money, as a debt or damages`                                -- s 6(1)(a)(i)
    `money on an equitable claim, money being the only relief`                -- s 6(1)(b)
    `the performance of work or services, or the return or replacement of goods`   -- only as a consumer/trader claim, s 7(3)(b)
    `possession of personal property unlawfully detained`                     -- s 6(1)(d), by its value
    `possession of real property`                                             -- s 6(1)(e), by its gross annual rental value
    `an indemnity arising from a claim before the Court`                      -- s 6(1)(g)

-- s 6(5): "Despite subsection (1), the Court does not have jurisdiction to deal with -- (a) a claim in which the title to land
-- is in question; (b) a claim in which a devise, bequest or limitation under a will or settlement is in question; (c) a claim
-- for damages for libel or slander; (d) a claim for damages for personal injury caused by or arising out of the use of a
-- motor vehicle; (e) a claim that the Building Commissioner or the State Administrative Tribunal has jurisdiction to deal
-- with under the Building Services (Complaint Resolution and Administration) Act 2011."
-- s 6(6): title coming "incidentally into question" does not oust jurisdiction; such a claim is `none of these`.
DECLARE `What my claim puts in question` IS ONE OF
    `none of these`
    `the title to land`
    `a devise, bequest or limitation under a will or settlement`
    `damages for libel or slander`
    `damages for personal injury from the use of a motor vehicle`
    `a building claim for the Building Commissioner or the State Administrative Tribunal`

DECLARE `My claim` HAS
    `what I am claiming`                                  IS A `What I am claiming`
    `the amount or value claimed, in dollars`             IS A NUMBER
    `what it puts in question`                            IS A `What my claim puts in question`
    `the other party consents to the Court dealing with it whatever the amount`   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(1) "consumer": the facts about me and the contract
    `I am a natural person`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `it arises from a contract with the other party`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `I bought or hired goods under it`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `services were supplied to me under it for a fee`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I contracted for resale or hire, for a business, or as a business partner`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a tenant under the Residential Tenancies Act 1987`   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(1), (2) "trader": the facts about the other party
    `the other party carries on a business of supplying goods or services, or regularly holds out to`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other party is a lessor under the Residential Tenancies Act 1987`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other party acted in a discipline not ordinarily regarded as trade or commerce`   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 26: whether it is a minor case
    `I elect the minor cases procedure`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties agree to treat it as a minor case`       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 28: whether it stays in the minor cases procedure
    `it involves jurisdiction conferred by a law of the Commonwealth`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `all the parties ask for the general procedure`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Court finds an important principle of law or complex facts or issues`   IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `s 7 -- consumer, trader, consumer/trader claim`

-- s 7(1): "consumer means a natural person -- (a) who buys or hires goods otherwise than -- (i) for resale or letting on hire;
-- or (ii) in the course of or for the purposes of a trade or business carried on, or to be carried on, by the person; or
-- (iii) as a member of a business partnership; or (b) for whom services are supplied for fee or reward otherwise than --
-- [the same business exclusions], but does not include a tenant within the meaning of the Residential Tenancies Act 1987
-- section 3".
-- Gloss: a private individual buying or hiring for themselves, not a business and not a residential tenant.
@export Am I a consumer for a consumer/trader claim (s 7(1))?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc Who you are, what the contract was for, and why you entered it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a consumer` IF
        `the claim`'s `I am a natural person`
    AND (`the claim`'s `I bought or hired goods under it` OR `the claim`'s `services were supplied to me under it for a fee`)
    AND (NOT (`the claim`'s `I contracted for resale or hire, for a business, or as a business partner`))
    AND (NOT (`the claim`'s `I am a tenant under the Residential Tenancies Act 1987`))

-- s 7(1): "trader means a person who in the field of trade or commerce carries on a business of supplying goods or providing
-- services or who regularly holds himself out as ready to supply goods or to provide services of a similar nature, but does
-- not include a lessor within the meaning of the Residential Tenancies Act 1987 section 3".
-- s 7(2): not a trader if, in supplying, the person "acts in the exercise of a discipline that is not ordinarily regarded as
-- being within the field of trade or commerce" (or carries out the instructions of one who does). Whether a discipline is of
-- that kind is a characterisation for the Court, asked as a fact.
@export Is the business I dealt with a trader for a consumer/trader claim (s 7(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What the other party does and in what capacity it supplied you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the other party a trader` IF
        `the claim`'s `the other party carries on a business of supplying goods or services, or regularly holds out to`
    AND (NOT (`the claim`'s `the other party is a lessor under the Residential Tenancies Act 1987`))
    AND (NOT (`the claim`'s `the other party acted in a discipline not ordinarily regarded as trade or commerce`))

-- s 7(3): "a consumer/trader claim is a claim -- (a) that arises out of a contract between a consumer and a trader for the
-- supply of goods or the provision of services; and (aa) that is made by the consumer or the trader against the other; and
-- (b) that claims one or more of the following -- (i) the performance of work, or the provision of services, of a value
-- that is not more than the jurisdictional limit; (ii) the payment, or the relief from payment, of an amount of money that
-- is not more than the jurisdictional limit; (iii) the return or replacement of goods of a value that is not more than the
-- jurisdictional limit."
-- In this seat the claim is made by the consumer against the trader, so (aa) is met when (a) is.
@export Is my claim against the business a consumer/trader claim (s 7(3))?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc Your claim against the business, what it seeks and its value
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim a consumer/trader claim` IF
        `the claim`'s `it arises from a contract with the other party`
    AND `Am I a consumer` `the claim`
    AND `Is the other party a trader` `the claim`
    AND (    `the claim`'s `what I am claiming` EQUALS `an amount of money, as a debt or damages`
          OR `the claim`'s `what I am claiming` EQUALS `the performance of work or services, or the return or replacement of goods`)
    AND `the claim`'s `the amount or value claimed, in dollars` AT MOST `the jurisdictional limit`

§§ `ss 6, 10 -- can the Magistrates Court hear my claim`

-- s 6(1)(a): a debt or damages "where the amount claimed, even if it is a balance after allowing for a payment on account or
-- for any admitted setoff or for any other amount, is not more than the jurisdictional limit"; (b) equitable money claims
-- under the same limit; (c) "a consumer/trader claim"; (d) personal property of value not more than the limit; (e) "subject
-- to the Residential Tenancies Act 1987", real property of gross annual rental value not more than the limit; (f) any of
-- (a) to (e) "irrespective of the amount claimed or the value of the property, if the party against which the claim is made
-- consents"; (g) an indemnity relating to another claim before the Court.
-- s 10(2): interest the Court may include under s 12, and judgment interest, "are to be disregarded".
DECLARE `Whether the Court can hear my claim` IS ONE OF
    `yes, within the general civil jurisdiction`
    `yes, as a consumer/trader claim`
    `yes, because the other party consents`
    `no: the Court has no jurisdiction over a claim of that kind (s 6(5))`
    `no: it is more than the jurisdictional limit`
    `no: only a consumer/trader claim can seek work, services, return or replacement`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the claim is excluded by s 6(5)` MEANS
    NOT (`the claim`'s `what it puts in question` EQUALS `none of these`)

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the claim is within the limit` MEANS
    `the claim`'s `the amount or value claimed, in dollars` AT MOST `the jurisdictional limit`

@export Can the Magistrates Court hear my claim, and on what footing (ss 6, 7, 10)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What you claim, its amount or value without interest, what it puts in question, and whether the other side consents
GIVETH A `Whether the Court can hear my claim`
DECIDE `Can the Magistrates Court hear my claim` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claim is excluded by s 6(5)` `the claim`
            THEN `no: the Court has no jurisdiction over a claim of that kind (s 6(5))`
        IF `Is my claim a consumer/trader claim` `the claim`
            THEN `yes, as a consumer/trader claim`
        IF `the claim`'s `what I am claiming` EQUALS `the performance of work or services, or the return or replacement of goods`
            THEN `no: only a consumer/trader claim can seek work, services, return or replacement`
        IF `the claim is within the limit` `the claim`
            THEN `yes, within the general civil jurisdiction`
        IF `the claim`'s `the other party consents to the Court dealing with it whatever the amount`
            THEN `yes, because the other party consents`
        OTHERWISE `no: it is more than the jurisdictional limit`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Court has jurisdiction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Can the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `the claim`
        WHEN `yes, within the general civil jurisdiction` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `yes, as a consumer/trader claim` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `yes, because the other party consents` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 26 -- minor case`

-- s 26: "minor case means -- (a) a claim within the jurisdiction of the Court where -- (i) the value of the claim or of the
-- relief claimed is not more than the minor cases jurisdictional limit; and (ii) the claimant has elected to have the claim
-- dealt with under the minor cases procedure; or ... (c) any other claim within the jurisdiction of the Court (including a
-- claim within the jurisdiction of the Court by virtue of a consent given under section 6(1)(f)) that the parties agree is
-- to be treated as a minor case."
-- s 16(1)(j): the Court may also order a case under the minor limit that the claimant did not elect into the minor cases
-- procedure; that is an order made later, not a fact the claimant states, and is not encoded.
@export Can I choose to bring my claim as a minor case (s 26(a))?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What you claim and its amount or value
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I bring my claim as a minor case` IF
        `the Court has jurisdiction` `the claim`
    AND `the claim`'s `the amount or value claimed, in dollars` AT MOST `the minor cases jurisdictional limit`

@export Is my claim a minor case (s 26)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc Your claim, and whether you elected the minor cases procedure or the parties agreed to it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim a minor case` IF
        (`Can I bring my claim as a minor case` `the claim` AND `the claim`'s `I elect the minor cases procedure`)
    OR  (`the Court has jurisdiction` `the claim` AND `the claim`'s `the parties agree to treat it as a minor case`)

§§ `ss 27, 28 -- which procedure my case follows`

-- s 27(1): "The primary object of the Court when dealing with a minor case is to attempt to bring the parties to a settlement
-- acceptable to all the parties." s 27(4): if it cannot, "the Court must deal with the minor case".
-- s 28(1): "The Court must deal with a minor case in accordance with the minor cases procedure unless an order has been made
-- under subsection (2) or (3)." (2): it "must order" the general procedure "if the case involves any jurisdiction conferred
-- on the Court by a law of the Commonwealth". (3): it "may order" the general procedure "if -- (a) all the parties so
-- request; or (b) the case involves an important principle of law or complex facts or issues". (3) is a discretion; it is
-- answered conditionally.
DECLARE `My procedure` IS ONE OF
    `the minor cases procedure`
    `the minor cases procedure, unless the Court orders the general procedure (s 28(3))`
    `the general procedure: the Court must order it for Commonwealth jurisdiction (s 28(2))`
    `the general procedure: it is not a minor case`
    `none: the Court cannot hear the claim`

@export Will my case be dealt with under the minor cases procedure or the general procedure (s 28)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc Your claim, whether it is a minor case, and whether it raises Commonwealth law, a request by all parties, or complexity
GIVETH A `My procedure`
DECIDE `Which procedure will my case follow` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the Court has jurisdiction` `the claim`))
            THEN `none: the Court cannot hear the claim`
        IF (NOT (`Is my claim a minor case` `the claim`))
            THEN `the general procedure: it is not a minor case`
        IF `the claim`'s `it involves jurisdiction conferred by a law of the Commonwealth`
            THEN `the general procedure: the Court must order it for Commonwealth jurisdiction (s 28(2))`
        IF `the claim`'s `all the parties ask for the general procedure`
            OR `the claim`'s `the Court finds an important principle of law or complex facts or issues`
            THEN `the minor cases procedure, unless the Court orders the general procedure (s 28(3))`
        OTHERWISE `the minor cases procedure`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the claim is in the minor cases procedure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Which procedure will my case follow` `the claim`
        WHEN `the minor cases procedure` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the minor cases procedure, unless the Court orders the general procedure (s 28(3))` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Will the magistrate first try to bring us to a settlement (s 27)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc Your claim and the procedure it follows
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Court first try to settle my case` IF
    `the claim is in the minor cases procedure` `the claim`

§§ `ss 29, 45 -- how the hearing is run`

-- s 29(1): minor case proceedings "are to be held in private unless the Court otherwise orders"; (2) "Relatives and friends of
-- a party may be present ... unless the Court otherwise orders"; (3) "as little formality as the Court thinks is reasonable";
-- (4) "the Court is not bound by rules or practice as to evidence but may inform itself on any matter in such manner as it
-- thinks fit".
-- s 45(1): otherwise proceedings "are to be conducted in open court unless this Act, the rules of court or another written
-- law provides otherwise".
@export Will my hearing be held in private (ss 29(1), 45(1))?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc Your claim and the procedure it follows
      `the Court has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has made an order changing the default (opening a minor case, or closing an ordinary one)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my hearing be in private` IS
    IF `the claim is in the minor cases procedure` `the claim`
        THEN (NOT `the Court has ordered otherwise`)
        ELSE `the Court has ordered otherwise`

@export Is the Court bound by the rules of evidence in my case (s 29(4))?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc Your claim and the procedure it follows
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Court bound by the rules of evidence` IF
    NOT (`the claim is in the minor cases procedure` `the claim`)

§§ `ss 30, 44 -- may a lawyer or someone else speak for me`

-- s 44(1): "A party to a case is personally entitled to appear before the Court in order to present and conduct the party's
-- case". (2): "Subject to section 30(2)", that may be done "(a) by a legal practitioner ... (d) with the Court's leave, by a
-- person who is not a legal practitioner"; (3): that leave only "in exceptional circumstances".
-- s 30(2): "Despite section 44(2), a party to a minor case is not entitled to be represented before the Court but ... (b) any
-- party may be represented by an agent with the leave of the Court given under this section."
-- s 30(4): "Except in the case of a consumer/trader claim", leave for a legal practitioner "(a) in proceedings prescribed under
-- subsection (3)(a); or (b) if all parties agree; or (c) if the Court is satisfied that it is in the interests of justice".
-- s 30(5): in a consumer/trader claim, leave for a legal practitioner "(a) if all parties agree; or (b) if the Court is
-- satisfied that none of the other parties will be unfairly disadvantaged as a result."
-- s 30(3): leave for an agent who is not a legal practitioner "(a) in proceedings, not being the trial of the case, if the
-- proceedings are prescribed by the regulations; or (b) in the trial of the case, if the Court considers that the party
-- should be given leave so that the party is not unfairly disadvantaged."
-- The Court's satisfaction and the regulations (not deposited) are inputs.
DECLARE `My request to be represented` HAS
    `all the parties agree`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Court is satisfied no other party will be unfairly disadvantaged`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Court is satisfied it is in the interests of justice`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the hearing is a proceeding prescribed by the regulations, not the trial`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Court considers I would otherwise be unfairly disadvantaged at the trial`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Court finds exceptional circumstances`                      IS A BOOLEAN

@export May a lawyer represent me in my case (ss 30(2), (4), (5), 44(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc Your claim, its procedure, and whether it is a consumer/trader claim
      `the request` IS A `My request to be represented` @desc Whether all parties agree and what the Court is satisfied of
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a lawyer represent me` IS
    IF NOT (`the claim is in the minor cases procedure` `the claim`)
        THEN TRUE
        ELSE IF `Is my claim a consumer/trader claim` `the claim`
            THEN     `the request`'s `all the parties agree`
                  OR `the request`'s `the Court is satisfied no other party will be unfairly disadvantaged`
            ELSE     `the request`'s `the hearing is a proceeding prescribed by the regulations, not the trial`
                  OR `the request`'s `all the parties agree`
                  OR `the request`'s `the Court is satisfied it is in the interests of justice`

@export May a friend or other non-lawyer represent me in my case (ss 30(3), 44(2)(d), (3))?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc Your claim and its procedure
      `the request` IS A `My request to be represented` @desc What the hearing is and what the Court considers
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a non-lawyer represent me` IS
    IF `the claim is in the minor cases procedure` `the claim`
        THEN     `the request`'s `the hearing is a proceeding prescribed by the regulations, not the trial`
              OR `the request`'s `the Court considers I would otherwise be unfairly disadvantaged at the trial`
        ELSE `the request`'s `the Court finds exceptional circumstances`

§§ `ss 25, 31 -- costs`

-- s 25(2): "A successful party is entitled to an order ... that the whole of its costs in the case be paid by the unsuccessful
-- party, unless the Court considers there is good reason not to make such an order or subsection (5) applies."
-- s 25(5): in a case where "(a) the value of the claim, or of the relief claimed, by the claimant is not more than the minor
-- cases jurisdictional limit; and (b) the claimant did not elect to have the claim dealt with under the minor cases procedure
-- or, under section 28(3), the court ordered that the case be dealt with under the general procedure", an order may be made
-- for a successful party only "if the order would be permitted by section 31 were the case being dealt with under the minor
-- cases procedure".
-- s 31(1): "allowable costs means -- (a) the court fees and service fees paid by a successful party; and (b) the costs of
-- enforcing a judgment." (2): a successful party to a minor case "is entitled to an order ... in relation to the party's
-- allowable costs but not in relation to the party's other costs". (3): other costs only if the Court "is satisfied that --
-- (a) because of the existence of exceptional circumstances an injustice would be done to the successful party if that
-- party's other costs were not ordered to be paid; or (b) the unsuccessful party's claim or defence was wholly without
-- merit; or (c)" [proceedings begun in a Local Court before 1 May 2005: spent, not encoded].
-- Encoder's reading: s 25(5) extends s 31 to every claim valued at or under the minor limit, elected or not; s 28(2)
-- orders are not named in s 25(5)(b), but such a claim is still a "minor case" under s 26 and so within s 31 itself.
DECLARE `The costs of the winner` IS ONE OF
    `the whole of the winner's costs, unless the Court finds good reason not to (s 25(2))`
    `only the allowable costs: court fees, service fees and enforcement costs (s 31(2))`
    `the allowable costs and the other costs, the Court being satisfied under s 31(3)`
    `none: the Court cannot hear the claim`

DECLARE `The costs findings` HAS
    `an injustice would be done in exceptional circumstances without the other costs`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the losing side's claim or defence was wholly without merit`                       IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 31 costs rule applies` MEANS
        `Is my claim a minor case` `the claim`
    OR  `the claim`'s `the amount or value claimed, in dollars` AT MOST `the minor cases jurisdictional limit`

@export What costs can the winner of my case be awarded against the loser (ss 25(2), (5), 31)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc Your claim, its value and whether it is a minor case
      `the findings` IS A `The costs findings` @desc What the Court is satisfied of about exceptional circumstances or a case wholly without merit
GIVETH A `The costs of the winner`
DECIDE `What costs can the winner recover` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the Court has jurisdiction` `the claim`)
            THEN `none: the Court cannot hear the claim`
        IF NOT (`the s 31 costs rule applies` `the claim`)
            THEN `the whole of the winner's costs, unless the Court finds good reason not to (s 25(2))`
        IF     `the findings`'s `an injustice would be done in exceptional circumstances without the other costs`
            OR `the findings`'s `the losing side's claim or defence was wholly without merit`
            THEN `the allowable costs and the other costs, the Court being satisfied under s 31(3)`
        OTHERWISE `only the allowable costs: court fees, service fees and enforcement costs (s 31(2))`

@export If I lose, could I be ordered to pay the other side's lawyer's fees (ss 25, 31)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc Your claim, its value and whether it is a minor case
      `the findings` IS A `The costs findings` @desc What the Court is satisfied of about exceptional circumstances or your claim being wholly without merit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Could I have to pay the other side's legal fees if I lose` IF
        (NOT (`What costs can the winner recover` `the claim` `the findings` EQUALS `only the allowable costs: court fees, service fees and enforcement costs (s 31(2))`))
    AND (NOT (`What costs can the winner recover` `the claim` `the findings` EQUALS `none: the Court cannot hear the claim`))

§§ `ss 32, 40 -- appeals`

-- s 32(1): "Except as provided by this section, no appeal lies against -- (a) an order made by the Court in the course of
-- proceedings in a minor case; or (b) the judgment of the Court in a minor case."
-- s 32(2): against the judgment, "(a) if the Court was constituted by a magistrate -- an appeal lies against the judgment
-- under Part 7 ...; or (b) if the Court was not constituted by a magistrate -- the party may appeal to a magistrate under and
-- subject to the rules of court".
-- s 32(3): only "on the grounds -- (a) that the minor case -- (i) was not within the jurisdiction of the Court; or (ii) was not
-- a minor case; or (b) that in dealing with the minor case there was a denial of natural justice; or (c) that the judgment was
-- beyond the Court's jurisdiction."
-- s 40(1): a party to a case "that is not a minor case" may appeal to the District Court against any order or the judgment;
-- (3) "An appeal cannot be commenced more than 21 days after the date of judgment, unless the District Court gives leave".
DECLARE `My ground of appeal` IS ONE OF
    `the case was not within the Court's jurisdiction`
    `the case was not a minor case`
    `I was denied natural justice`
    `the judgment was beyond the Court's jurisdiction`
    `the Court got the facts or the law wrong`

DECLARE `What I am appealing against` IS ONE OF
    `the judgment`
    `an order made in the course of the proceedings`

DECLARE `Who decided my case` IS ONE OF
    `a magistrate`
    `a registrar or other non-magistrate`

DECLARE `My appeal` IS ONE OF
    `no appeal lies (s 32)`
    `to the District Court under Part 7 (ss 32(2)(a), 40)`
    `to a magistrate, under the rules of court (s 32(2)(b))`
    `to the District Court (s 40(1))`

GIVEN `ground` IS A `My ground of appeal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a minor case ground` MEANS
    NOT (`ground` EQUALS `the Court got the facts or the law wrong`)

@export Can I appeal, and to which court (ss 32, 40(1))?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc Your claim and the procedure it followed
      `against` IS A `What I am appealing against` @desc The judgment, or an order made along the way
      `decided by` IS A `Who decided my case` @desc Whether a magistrate or a registrar decided it
      `ground` IS A `My ground of appeal` @desc Why you say the decision is wrong
GIVETH A `My appeal`
DECIDE `Can I appeal and to whom` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the claim is in the minor cases procedure` `the claim`)
            THEN `to the District Court (s 40(1))`
        IF `against` EQUALS `an order made in the course of the proceedings`
            THEN `no appeal lies (s 32)`
        IF NOT (`is a minor case ground` `ground`)
            THEN `no appeal lies (s 32)`
        IF `decided by` EQUALS `a magistrate`
            THEN `to the District Court under Part 7 (ss 32(2)(a), 40)`
        OTHERWISE `to a magistrate, under the rules of court (s 32(2)(b))`

-- s 40(3): 21 days, unless the District Court gives leave. The time for an appeal from a registrar to a magistrate is set by
-- the rules of court, which are not deposited: answered NOTHING.
@export How many days after the judgment do I have to start my appeal (s 40(3))?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc Your claim and the procedure it followed
      `against` IS A `What I am appealing against` @desc The judgment, or an order made along the way
      `decided by` IS A `Who decided my case` @desc Whether a magistrate or a registrar decided it
      `ground` IS A `My ground of appeal` @desc Why you say the decision is wrong
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days do I have to appeal` IS
    CONSIDER `Can I appeal and to whom` `the claim` `against` `decided by` `ground`
        WHEN `to the District Court (s 40(1))` THEN JUST 21
        WHEN `to the District Court under Part 7 (ss 32(2)(a), 40)` THEN JUST 21
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
